{%- comment -%}
  One background video, emitted the same way everywhere on the page.

  Two things this fixes versus the Korean markup:

  1. Poster resolution. KR points at the `_small` preview frame, which is about
     3 KB and visibly soft — and it is what the visitor looks at until the video
     is playing. This upgrades it to the 1024px rendition (~90 KB), or the full
     frame for the hero.

  2. Loading. The KR page starts fetching every video at once. With a dozen
     background videos competing, the one on screen arrives last and stalls,
     which reads as bad quality. Here the source is held in data-src and
     attached by sidiz-video.js only as the video nears the viewport, so the
     visible video gets the bandwidth.

  Accepts:
    url     - mp4 URL (required)
    poster  - poster image URL
    alt     - describes the footage, used as aria-label
    classes - extra classes, e.g. 'web' / 'mobile'
    eager   - true for the hero video only
    size    - poster rendition: 'full' | '1024' (default)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign poster_url = poster

  # KR serves preview frames as <name>.thumbnail.<n>_small.jpg. The suffix is
  # what makes it tiny, so swap it for a usable rendition.
  if poster_url contains '_small.'
    assign wanted = '_1024x.'
    if size == 'full'
      assign wanted = '.'
    endif
    assign poster_url = poster_url | replace: '_small.', wanted
  endif

  assign is_eager = false
  if eager == true or eager == 'true'
    assign is_eager = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if url != blank -%}
  <video
    data-sidiz-video
    {% if is_eager %}data-eager="true"{% endif %}
    class="{{ classes }}"
    playsinline="playsinline"
    autoplay="autoplay"
    loop="loop"
    muted="muted"
    preload="none"
    disableremoteplayback
    {% if poster_url != blank %}poster="{{ poster_url }}"{% endif %}
    {% if alt != blank %}aria-label="{{ alt | escape }}"{% endif %}
  >
    <source data-src="{{ url }}" type="video/mp4">
    {%- if poster_url != blank -%}
      <img src="{{ poster_url }}" alt="{{ alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    {%- endif -%}
  </video>
{%- endif -%}
